## Operator tools the audit added — know these

These are theme-local helpers you'll use weekly:

### `nav_admin_warn($code, $message)` — `inc/compliance.php`
Push a backend warning to a transient queue that surfaces as a dismissible WP admin notice on the next dashboard load. Bounded at 20 unique codes, 7-day TTL, `manage_options`-gated. Currently fires on:
- JSON-LD encode failures
- `update_post_meta()` failures during product save (COA / batch / lab fields)
- `_nav_meta_description` save failures
- `wp_insert_term()` failures during theme activation
- Missing `privacy-policy` / `terms-of-service` pages

**When debugging, check wp-admin first.** The codebase logs to `error_log` AND surfaces to admin notices for compliance-critical paths.

### `nav_redact($value)` — `inc/compliance.php`
Returns a 12-char SHA-256 token salted by `AUTH_SALT`. Use for any IP / email / UA value going to `error_log`. NEVER log raw PII — GDPR + Argyle audit risk.

### `nav_subscriber_pii_scrub` cron — `inc/subscribe.php`
Daily scheduled event. Deletes `_nav_ip_hash` + `_nav_user_agent_hash` from `nav_subscriber` rows older than 365 days. Email + consent timestamp stay. Filterable via `nav_subscriber_pii_retention_days`. Scheduled on `after_switch_theme`, cleared on `switch_theme`.

### `nav_get_disclaimer('sitewide')` — `inc/compliance.php`
Single source of truth for the RUO line. Every call-site resolves to the same string. If you need a different disclaimer, add a key — don't paraphrase inline.

### SEO meta box — `inc/seo.php`
Every page/post/product has a "SEO — Navigate Peptides" meta box with two fields:
- **Meta Description** override (160-char target, falls back to auto-generated)
- **Social Share Image (Open Graph)** — media picker, stores `_nav_og_image_id`. Falls back to featured image → theme OG fallback.

### `nav_seo_scrub($text)` — `inc/seo.php`
Compliance regex rewriter. Applied to every product description, term description, meta description, schema description, OG description. Map at `inc/seo.php:90-130`. Add to it; don't bypass it.

