### Debugging

#### Site looks broken after deploy
1. wp-admin dashboard → look for `nav_admin_warn` notices
2. Browser console on the live URL → JS errors
3. `view-source:` → check for orphaned `<%1$s>` placeholders, missing JSON-LD
4. Revert the offending PR if obvious; the workflow re-deploys automatically

#### JSON-LD validation fails on Google rich-results test
`nav_seo_json_ld()` logs encode failures via `error_log` AND surfaces them via `nav_admin_warn`. Check wp-admin first. Then run the page through https://search.google.com/test/rich-results.

#### WC checkout shows literal `%1$s` text near privacy link
`nav_privacy_url()` returned empty. Verify the privacy-policy page exists with slug `privacy-policy` or `privacy`. The handler (PR #99) emits an admin notice when this happens.

#### Model-viewer canvas is transparent on a PDP
Browser console → look for CSP-blocked fetches. Likely a regression in `functions.php`'s CSP allowlist. Verify `ajax.googleapis.com` is in `connect-src`. Post-PR #99, model-viewer errors fire a GA4 `model_viewer_error` event too.

#### 3D vial label looks wrong
The label is an embedded image on the GLB material. To re-render: see `/tmp/build-ghkcu-label.py` archived in the project history (Pillow-based). Update the label PNG, then re-bake via `/tmp/regreen-all-vials.py` (Blender headless). The pipeline is described in commit messages on PRs #88–#90.

