## Things you'll want to do in your first week

1. **Read `docs/COMPLIANCE`** end to end. Internalize the forbidden vocab. The `nav_seo_scrub()` map is your safety net but not a substitute for knowing the rules.
2. **Get wp-admin access from Ian** — Editor role minimum, Administrator if you're going to be the maintainer. Set up a dedicated user, don't share Ian's.
3. **Get GitHub repo access** — push to `main` triggers deploy; PRs are reviewable.
4. **Generate an SSH key**, send the public half to Ian for wp.com Calypso registration. Test direct SSH to the live site with `wp --version` before relying on it for anything else.
5. **Walk every public page** with your eyes — homepage, /compounds/, every category, every PDP, /quality/* subpages, /about/, /contact/, /cart/, /checkout/ (test mode). Note anything off; many of those pages were reviewed by audit but not by human eyes recently.
6. **Run Lighthouse + Google rich-results test** on the homepage and a PDP. Establish a baseline.
7. **Check wp-admin → Site Health** — should be green; if not, that's your first ticket.

